course: dictionary
lesson: 11393
title: Accelerate: going faster, or sooner
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Accelerate is a verb. Its most common meaning is to go faster, or to make something go faster: «The car accelerated along the motorway.» The clue is the motorway. Cars on a motorway go fast, so accelerated must mean sped up.
explain: Accelerate can also mean to make something happen sooner or more quickly: «Rain accelerated the rusting of the old gate.» The gate was not moving. The rain made the rust arrive faster, so the word is about time, not speed.
explain: In science lessons, accelerate has a wider meaning. It means changing velocity, which can be speeding up, slowing down or changing direction. So «Gravity makes the stone accelerate» means the stone's speed changes as it falls.
fact: Accelerate means to go faster, or to make something go faster.
fact: Accelerate can also mean to make something happen sooner or more quickly.
fact: In science, accelerate means changing velocity, which includes speeding up, slowing down or changing direction.
fact: «Accelerate away» means to speed off quickly.
exercise: «The bus accelerated away from the stop.» What does accelerated mean here? | Stopped suddenly | Turned into a field | Honked loudly | *Went faster
exercise: «Rust is destroying the bridge, and the wet weather has accelerated it.» What does accelerated suggest? | *Made it happen sooner | Stopped it completely | Painted over it | Made it colder
exercise: In science, a stone falling down a hill will accelerate. What does that mean? | It floats in the air | It stays at exactly the same speed | *Its speed or direction is changing | It only moves backwards
test: «Drivers must not accelerate near schools.» Why is this a safety rule? | Cars must be quiet near schools | Drivers should sing near schools | *Going faster near children is dangerous | Schools need faster cars
test: A cyclist wants to get away from a barking dog as fast as possible. Which word fits best? | dissolve | whisper | slumber | *accelerate away
exam: «The engine accelerated, then slowed, then turned left.» Which statement about accelerate is correct? | Accelerate is a noun for a car part | Accelerate only ever means to go faster | Accelerate means to stop completely | *In science, accelerate can mean speeding up, slowing down or changing direction
